    "body": "Found by the Review 5 unit-economics stress test (2026-07-03). The cost pipeline (ADR 0023 / cost-telemetry + cost-anomaly workers) is not producing data at any link of the chain:\n\n1. **No per-customer D1 databases exist.** \\`wrangler d1 list\\` shows none, and \\`customer_configs.connectors_json.per_customer_d1_database_id\\` is NULL for both live seats — so the daily ingest cron skips 100% of customers by design (\\`workers/cost-telemetry/src/index.ts:44-72\\`). \\`cost_telemetry\\` and \\`captain_time_events\\` (the only labor instrumentation) have nowhere to write. \\`cost_anomaly_alerts\\` is empty.\n2. **The Anthropic usage API rejects our key.** \\`/v1/organizations/usage_report/messages\\` requires an Admin API key; the \\`/ss\\` vault has only the runtime \\`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY\\` (verified: \\`authentication_error\\`). Even with D1s provisioned, ingest 401s. Needs an \\`ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY\\` provisioned and the worker secret set.\n3. **Attribution is org-level.** \\`fetchDailyUsage()\\` calls the usage API with one org key and writes the same org-wide totals into *each* customer's DB — per-seat COGS cannot be isolated. Fix direction: per-customer Anthropic workspaces (workspace_id grouping on the usage API) or per-seat keys.\n4. 15 of the 17 spec'd drivers (Fly, D1, R2, Vectorize, AgentMail, ...) are phase-2 stubs — known/accepted, listed for completeness.\n\n**Decision needed before build:** provision per-customer D1s + admin key + workspace attribution as designed, or re-point v1 at a single central table (simpler, still ADR 0009-compliant since it holds SMD-side billing metadata, not customer data). Related: the COGS/MRR kill gate (>40% two consecutive months) is unarmed both because of this and because no Operator price is authored (#1659).\n\nThe opus-4-8 zero-costing bug found in the same review was fixed in #1658.",
